# Refresh tokens live in an httpOnly cookie. In VS Code REST Client the cookie is kept
# between requests automatically, so run Login first, then Refresh.

POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "Sonic@gmail.com",
  "password": "Sonic123"
}

### Refresh (rotates the cookie, returns a new access token)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/refresh

### Logout (revokes this session)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/logout
